{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Save me</b> — corresponding to the tearing and roaring lion." "<b>And the meaning of my only one</b> — because every soul of man is a singular unit, isolated with its body from the universal soul, and upon separation from its body, it is gathered to the whole." "<b>And the meaning of from the horns of re'em</b> — for they are stronger than all horns. And I have heard certain people say that the re'em throws itself from a high mountain onto its horns and they do not break. And ראמים is missing alef, like בחמה (in heat)." "<b>And the meaning of You answered me</b> — for You have already done me kindness from a distress like this." "<b>And the meaning of from my horns</b> — as if I were upon his horns. And some say: for his horns are higher than all horns; and the proof: 'and his horn is exalted like that of a re'em' (Psalms 92:11)." "<b>And the meaning of You answered me</b> — corresponding to 'I call by day and You do not answer' (Psalms 22:3)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra reads ראמים as defective spelling of ראימים; the comparison to בחמה illustrates a word where alef has dropped. I have not expanded the grammatical point beyond his terse formulation.", 4 "Ibn Ezra implies ותרם כראם קרני as his proof text, which aligns with the received text of Psalms 92:11."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:19.683591806Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}